  "claim_short": "Remark 18 Q_+ positive orbit extreme-point hull transitivity. New partial theorem: if z*=a x* for a nonincreasing multiplier a in [0,1], then z belongs to Q_+(x) and Q_+(z) is contained in Q_+(x). Dyadic lower approximants express a x* as norm limits of convex combinations of initial-interval extreme points, without order continuity. Also records literature-implied full zero-dilation subcases from source Theorems...",
